WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.222
This mini project brings the whole module together.

00:00:03.222 --> 00:00:10.927
Sales are forty-two hundred dollars, costs are thirty-one hundred dollars, and the tax rate is six percent.

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:14.972
Profit is eleven hundred. Tax is sixty-six.

00:00:14.972 --> 00:00:18.857
Net profit becomes one thousand thirty-four dollars.

00:00:18.857 --> 00:00:25.899
Then net profit is divided by sales to get a net margin of about twenty-four point six percent.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:35.410
Notice how many Module 1 ideas appear here: meaningful variables, numeric types, arithmetic, derived metrics, f-strings,

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.985
money formatting, and percentages.

00:00:37.985 --> 00:00:46.513
Change one input, predict which outputs should move, and then run the code to verify your reasoning.
